WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:01.234
[SOUNDS OF ROOSTERS

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:10.176
AND LIVESTOCK]

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:16.716
Yvon, I'll meet
you on the path.

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:18.218
Keep a close eye on him.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.191
ELISHA COOKE: You've
encountered Mr. Cross.

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:26.192
HAMISH GOAMES: I have.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:31.131
ELISHA COOKE: Well?

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.867
What did he have
to say for himself?

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:35.268
HAMISH GOAMES: Riddles.

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:37.303
He's not the same man I knew.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.973
Well that's a fortunate
outcome at least.

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:42.675
Not for my sister.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:46.513
It's natural that a place like
this should transform a man.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:51.818
I find myself anew in the silver
of the mirror every morning.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:54.854
Now, I take it you spoke to
Captain Wale in Quebec City.

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:00.627
This is Mr. Charles Duquet.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.495
You may speak freely
in front of him.

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:06.866
[horse whinnying]

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:10.870
[inaudible], good to meet you.

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:17.477
I did not come
here for tea, and I

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:20.180
prefer molasses, not honey.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:23.249
Captain Wale did confirm
your ties to the company.

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:25.585
Well, you see, I am a
man who speaks plainly.

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:29.756
We found Lafarge's boy.

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:36.663
ELISHA COOKE: Now
that is a relief.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:42.435
Well, it would be,
if he were still alive.

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:46.806
We found him dead, by the river.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:49.342
A shame.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:52.445
His mother will be
brought to her knees.

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:55.415
The boy's death
is on your ledger.

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:57.817
ELISHA COOKE: No, Mr. Goames.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:58.952
You're mistaken.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.119
I have orders
from Captain Wale

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:02.121
to form a partnership with you.

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:06.759
And though I find
it disagreeable,

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:12.065
I am a company man, and an
order is an order after all.

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:15.969
But I but a
simple barrel-maker.

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:18.671
My position within these walls
hinges on the good graces

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:19.973
of [inaudible].

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:21.374
You see my time in
the fiddle afforded

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:22.742
me some much needed reflection.

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:24.711
I am keeping my beard
low to the ground,

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:27.213
and as such, I would
point you in the direction

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:30.350
of a Mr. Bill Selby.

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:31.751
He's out there,
forming alliances.

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:35.455
Perhaps your Mr. Cross
knows of his whereabouts.

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:39.659
Good day.

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.146
I handled the boy.

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:04.050
And left the body for
only passing fool to find.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:05.351
Better it look
like an accident.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:08.721
It was an accident, Charles.

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:10.189
I see it in your eyes.

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:11.958
It was sloppy work.

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:14.327
I should dissolve
our partnership.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:20.066
That would be an
unfortunate decision.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.668
It's my decision to make!

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:28.508
Before you make
it, I would like

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:31.110
to know why you neglected
to tell the Hudson's

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.412
Bay men about the pistols.

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:39.252
What pistols are
you referring to?

00:03:51.798 --> 00:03:55.134
If I were going to betray
you, I already would have.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.775
When I found that
letter on your desk,

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:06.245
I gleamed a lot about your
arrangement to supply guns

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:07.680
to the Hudson's Bay Company.

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:14.554
But I must confess, I am still
curious on a couple of points.

00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:21.094
It seems I misjudged you.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.895
Where are the pistols?

00:04:22.962 --> 00:04:24.330
I don't know.

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:25.698
They were to arm the
Iroquois so that they could

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:26.733
use them against the French.

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:33.506
I know not what they
were intended for.

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:38.211
I traded for them,
took my profit.

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:39.345
That's the end of the story.

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:47.453
Good, good.

